WEBVTT

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.270
What? He slipped and fell?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.770
- 1337, wasn't it?
- You think he'll be okay?

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.070
This kind of thing
happens to him all the time.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.160
Well, 1337 is still a Spartan.
He's been trained with the best of them.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.070
There's no need for concern.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.290
If you say so, Master Chief.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.500
It wouldn't be the first time
he fell off a Pelican.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.460
- But still, I am a little worried.
- Yeah.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.710
Oh, no.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.090
Hey! Wait for me! Come back!

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.930
Don't leave me behind!

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.470
I'm gonna have to rendezvous with them
somewhere.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.890
Huh?

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.980
I wonder if these natives are dangerous?

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.320
Hey, look at that.
It's the junky old robot that fell.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.690
Ha-ha-ha. I am not some junky robot.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.490
Even if you don't wanna know,
I'll tell you who I am.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.530
I am one of the strongest warriors
in space.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.540
I am Spartan-1337.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.210
- I wouldn't stand there if I were you.
- It's not safe.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.120
How dare they ignore
my awesome heroism.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.840
Fear not. I am the strongest warrior
in the... Oh, no.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.890
I'm fine. That was just a few dents.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.610
He doesn't really get along with strangers
all that much.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:59.450
So where is the accursed group
of Spartans?

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.870
On Cronkee,
the fourth planet of the Unicon system.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.950
Excellent.
This is the perfect opportunity...

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.710
...to show those Spartans a thing or two
about Covenant power.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.260
- Bring out Pluton.
- Yes, sir.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.050
Yes. It is the finest bio-warrior
ever created.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.680
Now go to the planet Cronkee
and demonstrate our might.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.430
But Pluton's weapons
are still in the experimental stage.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.230
They'll be enough
to vanquish the humans.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.860
Don't you think a real battle
will be the best way...

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.900
...to conduct our little test?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.440
If that is your wish.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.570
I will get you at long last, Master Chief.
Now go, Pluton!

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.580
- Guh.
- Not "guh." Go destroy them!

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.750
No, not over here.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.080
- He's over that way. He's over there!
- Huh?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.580
Don't "huh" me. Go that way.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.090
I need a vacation.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.140
Chief, respond please.
Can you hear me? Chief? Over.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.810
There's some strange interference.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.940
- Hello? Can you hear me?
- We can hear you.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.900
Not you. And I thought I told you
to stop following me.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.030
- Robot, look.
- I told you I'm not a robot.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.460
What's that?

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.970
Sure is a lot of junk
falling from the sky today.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.020
Covenant? It's dangerous.
Get out of here!

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.310
- As far as you can.
- Okay.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.770
Chief, this... Stop it. Stop it.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.460
Are you guys all right?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.380
- Hey, look. It's big brother.
- And big sister.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.220
Any of you know
what that thing is?

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.720
It looks like he almost blew up
the mountain range.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:12.720
He fell from the sky. All of a sudden, he
and this giant monkey started going nuts.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.430
Don't worry.
Your big brother is gonna take care of it.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.560
Yeah. Well, he might be a little tougher
than you think.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.570
We don't have much choice.
We'll just have to try our best.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.230
Yeah, you might lose.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.900
Why would you say that?
Give me some credit, will you?

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:29.070
It must have been scary.
Are you sure you're okay?

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.820
I'm kind of hungry.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.120
All right, let's do this.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:41.290
I'm not gonna lose. No way can I lose.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:46.590
I am Spartan-1337.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.140
No one else will say it, so I will.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:58.270
The fact that I never give up
is one of my good points!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.060
Hey, look. The rain stopped.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.690
The robot's back.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.440
What's that?

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:09.610
Apparently they used to travel
between the stars with that.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.820
An old UNSC frigate.
Must've crash-landed.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.410
I hear that we were all born inside there.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.080
Mama raised us all by herself.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.540
Mama?

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.500
You kids should stay behind.
This is my fight.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.840
Don't worry about it. We may
not look it, but we're pretty tough.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.880
Though, we're no match for Mama.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.090
Mama, huh?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.550
When we were still little
she fought off a bunch...

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.390
...of bird-headed pirates by herself.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.810
That sounds like one heck of a mama.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:39.850
But you know what?

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.020
I'm one heck of a mama myself.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.680
I did it.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.850
I did it!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.230
Oh, no. We'll be done for
if he reaches full strength.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.230
- We gotta stop him.
- Yeah, and that's gonna be the hard part.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.520
Less talk, more action.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.080
Ah!

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:59.100
This isn't good. He won't budge.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.310
We're totally screwed.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:02.770
What else can we do?

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.230
We're doomed.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.400
Well, don't jinx us!

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:07.730
I'm just kidding.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.070
We gotta do something.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.400
Hey, what the heck is that?

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.160
Oh, as if he'd ever fall for that.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.620
He did fall for it.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:22.750
He did? He did.
Now let's get out of here.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.430
Whoa. What's happening?

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.600
No way.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.150
Ah!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.940
Is that a Slipspace rupture?

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.700
Ah!

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.130
That was Mama.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.220
I told you, no one was as tough as Mama.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.300
Master Chief, radio contact
has been reestablished.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.140
Good. I'll try to contact 1337.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.730
There's another Al living on this planet.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:29.100
- What?
- I've lost contact with it.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:33.860
But I'm pretty sure I felt it just tinkering
with the Slipspace drive.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.740
She's another Al it seems. Just like I am.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.030
Why here?

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.200
- You want me to collect her?
- No. Let's not do that.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:45.580
It's a very old Al construct.
You might say something of an antique.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.000
- She seems...
- Seems what?

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:53.840
Happy. If I'm understanding correctly,
she seems to be happy here. Hm.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.260
Hm.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.130
We're home.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.430
Were you playing as cavemen
again? You really do like that game.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.930
Mama, you're not gonna believe
what happened today.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.600
All right, all right.
You can tell me all about that later.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.770
Mama, just what did you do back there?

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.060
That's not important right now.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.730
By the way, dinner is ready.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.570
- I'm hungry.
- I thought so.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.240
- Now go wash your hands.
- Okay.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.360
And clean behind your ears.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.120
Mama.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.790
Can you hear me, 1337? Come in, 1337.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.170
This is 1337. I hear you clearly, sir.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:36.380
Head to the rendezvous point immediately.
Rendezvous ASAP, over.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:42.550
Huh? Roger that, sir,
but I may run a little late!

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:58.740
Guh.
